module Main

import Prelude

-- A cell's header counts its object slots in 8 bits, so 255 counted
-- references are the most the header itself counts; a cell of more holds
-- their count in a word after it. Three records of strings, each in a tree
-- built from input and freed, every field with it:
--
-- * R254 is unboxed, so its 254 strings go into the cell of N254 with
--   N254's tail: 255, which the header counts.
-- * R256's 256 strings are its constructor's own fields, more than the
--   header counts, so a box of R256, which leaves N256 one reference, is a
--   cell whose count of them is a word after its header.
-- * R512's 512 are as many again, a count whose low 8 bits are those of 0.
--
-- Each record holds strings of their own in its first and last fields and
-- in those on either side of the count's 8-bit edge (253 to 256), so a slot
-- read from the wrong place shows; `ends` reads them back from every node.

